  "title": "NS -- Recompose The Momentum Network To The Reference Design",
  "type": "feature",
  "userRequest": "Feature: NS -- Recompose The Momentum Network To The Reference Design\n\nProject context: We need to modernize the https://www.harvardintech.com/ website from the outside. The site was built with a no-code product so we need to faithfully reproduce it using modern technologies and host it as a GitHub pages website. It also needs a CRM that can be run locally or, ideally also in the cloud via GitHub pages as well (protected with a password and/or GitHub OAuth). Can we dig into this?",
  "description": "The Momentum Network became the hero of /donate, opening the page in place of the photo hero at the team's direction, and the recognition band was pulled out of the reorderable flow to hold that position — Order and Draft no longer move or hide it, the same contract the closing ask already had, while its Kicker and Heading stay editable. The `?name=` greeting the old hero carried was restored rather than lost with it: `applyNetworkGreeting` fills `heroHeadlineNamed` in the browser and reveals a gold line above the grid headline, so a subscriber arriving from the campaign email is greeted by name while the public visitor sees the signed-off design untouched — an additive line, not a headline swap, because the headline is the composition. Two suite failures the runner attributed to inherited base debt were traced to this branch instead and fixed: the new momentumSections schema keys (raised / goal / percent / ctaLabel) had no CMS editor inputs, breaking the fully-editable guarantee, and the @codeyam/cms 0.13.0 upgrade reworked the unbacked-media guard from refusing before any network call to probing each candidate and refusing the 404s.",
